# v3.1.9.10 RC (part A: backup retention tiers + per-message chat journal).
# A copy of Dockerfile.v3199 (everything below its own header is unchanged
# except: image tags, the new COPY of compactor/chatjournal.py, and the
# import guard, which now lists 29 modules). The header that follows is the
# v3.1.9.9 one, still accurate for the base chain and the rollback stage.
#
# v3.1.9.9 RC — multi-stage build, 2026-09-27. Same base chain as
# Dockerfile.v3198 (prod's actual running image, NOT the c1295894 chain the
# original v3198 RC used) — see that file's own header for the full
# rebuild rationale, still accurate here since the `rollback` stage below
# is byte-for-byte the same recipe. The ONLY thing v3.1.9.9 adds on top of
# .8 is cloudflared, baked into the `rc` stage (task: give her OpenWebUI a
# stable https://ai.revelationsaints.com URL via a Cloudflare Tunnel,
# instead of the RunPod proxy URL). See docker/cloudflared-run.sh and
# RUNBOOK_CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL.md for the rest of the tunnel design.
#
# BACKGROUND (why the .8 rebuild happened, unchanged from Dockerfile.v3198):
# the earlier Dockerfile.v3198 was a thin layer on local/zla:v3197-rc, itself built FROM
# angreg/zions-light-ai@sha256:c1295894dd585784611c6833b1d4c396880ac8723e6b9b46531a5aa846cb8a65
# — v3.1.9.4/.5/.6, tagged but NEVER DEPLOYED (memory.md, "PRODUCTION RUNS
# v3.1.9"). Prod actually runs angreg/zions-light-ai:v3.1.9-cu12
# (sha256:f3fafa3e1949115dfd2c1354969b03be8d852fc491b647884ccfe7a23cf998d2),
# with OpenWebUI hot-patched to 0.11.4 IN THE RUNNING CONTAINER'S OVERLAY
# ONLY — never baked into any image, and reverted by any pod restart. A
# hostile review found the old RC's vllm-venv/compactor-venv ship a
# DIFFERENT package set from what prod's image actually has installed
# (openai, filelock 4, urllib3, protobuf, huggingface_hub, cuda-pathfinder,
# opencv-python-headless and others) — a set that has never run vLLM on a
# real GPU — and shares NO layers with prod, so the pod would pull ~11 GB
# on deploy instead of the few new-layer MB this rebuild produces. The
# rollback path also needs to boot an image that is BYTE-FOR-BYTE equal to
# what a pod running today would fall back to: prod's baked bits
# (f3fafa3e) plus the SAME OpenWebUI 0.11.4 pip upgrade already live on
# prod's overlay — not a different lineage that merely happens to also
# carry 0.11.4.
#
# BASE CHAIN (this file):
#   angreg/zions-light-ai@sha256:f3fafa3e1949115dfd2c1354969b03be8d852fc491b647884ccfe7a23cf998d2
#     (prod's actual, currently-running image; `docker images --digests` /
#     `docker inspect --format='{{json .RepoDigests}}'` on the pulled
#     `v3.1.9-cu12` tag, confirmed 2026-09-27)
#   --[stage `rollback`, this file]--> local/zla:v31910-rollback
#     OpenWebUI bumped 0.11.0 -> 0.11.4 in /app/venv, EXACTLY the same
#     install/strip/cleanup recipe Dockerfile.v3197 uses against the OLD
#     base — and NOTHING else. UNCHANGED from Dockerfile.v3198's own
#     `rollback` stage (same base digest, same recipe, byte-for-byte) —
#     only the stage's own image tag differs, because it now lives in this
#     file. This stage IS the rollback target: it is defined to equal
#     prod's live state (baked image + the in-place OpenWebUI patch), so
#     that rolling a .9 deploy back means booting something that already
#     matches what prod is running right now, not a step backward to some
#     other lineage. It also has NO cloudflared binary and NO
#     [program:cloudflared] — rolling back also rolls back the tunnel,
#     which is correct: the rollback target is "what a pod running today
#     would fall back to", and today's pod has no tunnel.
#   --[stage `rc`, this file]--> local/zla:v31910-rc
#     FROM rollback. Adds everything Dockerfile.v3198's `rc` stage added
#     (the v3197 scroll-jump custom.css append; every non-test
#     compactor/*.py module — request tracing + word-ban file-deploy
#     runtime; ops/ and scripts/ baked to /opt/zl-repo; entrypoint.sh and
#     supervisord.conf, which DO differ from prod's baked copies; the
#     import guard, 29 modules as of .10) PLUS ONE NEW THING: cloudflared, baked from
#     the official GitHub release, pinned by sha256, installed to
#     /usr/local/bin/cloudflared, plus docker/cloudflared-run.sh baked to
#     /opt/cloudflared-run.sh. See the CLOUDFLARED section near the end of
#     this stage.
#
# stt/server.py, tts/server.py, both venvs' requirements.txt, and
# clean-models.sh were extracted from a throwaway container of
# f3fafa3e1949 (`docker cp`) and `cmp`'d BYTE-IDENTICAL to this tree's
# copies (2026-09-27) — none are COPYd here; the base image's own files are
# already correct. entrypoint.sh and supervisord.conf were diffed the same
# way and DO differ (D1/D2/D3/D5/D6/D11/D12/D14 fixes plus the new
# [program:zl-ops] stanza), so both are COPYd below.
#
# COMPACTOR-VENV: ONE PACKAGE ADDED, opencv-python-headless==5.0.0.93 (--no-deps).
# compactor/requirements.txt has pinned it since v3.1.9.3 (mistral_common's
# image tokenizer imports cv2). Prod's compactor-venv (f3fafa3e) predates the
# pin, so an image-bearing request's token count falls back to a rough
# estimate there. Every .8 test and review ran on images that HAD this
# package in compactor-venv, so the rc stage installs exactly that pinned
# version, with --no-deps (numpy 2.3.5 is already present), to ship the
# tested configuration. The rc stage then runs `pip check`. Nothing else in
# any venv differs from prod except /app/venv (the OpenWebUI 0.11.4 upgrade).
#
# TO BUILD EACH TARGET:
#   docker build --target rollback -t local/zla:v31910-rollback -f Dockerfile.v31910 .
#   docker build --target rc       -t local/zla:v31910-rc       -f Dockerfile.v31910 .
# (both from this repo's root as the build context; .dockerignore keeps
# tests/, docs, and __pycache__/*.pyc at every depth out of that context)

# =============================================================================
# Stage: rollback — prod's live state (f3fafa3e baked bits + the same
# OpenWebUI 0.11.4 pip upgrade already hot-patched onto prod's overlay).
# Nothing else changes here. Compare against
# ~/zl-ops/v3198/rc-review-B/hp/Dockerfile (the reviewer's own minimal
# recipe for this exact stage) — same base tag, same constraint file, same
# `pip install open-webui==0.11.4 -c <constraints>`; this stage additionally
# matches Dockerfile.v3197's strip/cleanup steps so the resulting /app/venv
# is byte-for-byte comparable to that recipe's lineage, not just
# "some 0.11.4 install".
# =============================================================================
FROM angreg/zions-light-ai@sha256:f3fafa3e1949115dfd2c1354969b03be8d852fc491b647884ccfe7a23cf998d2 AS rollback

# Same constraints file Dockerfile.v3197 pins the 0.11.0 -> 0.11.4 bump
# with (docs/v3197-pip-diff.txt documents what it was derived from). Reused
# as-is: the OpenWebUI version target is identical here, so the transitive
# pins that matter are identical too.
COPY docs/v3197-constraints.txt /tmp/v3197-constraints.txt

# Recipe copied verbatim from Dockerfile.v3197 (M-5, review1-v3197-65ea196):
# `touch` a marker BEFORE the pip install, then scope the `strip` to files
# `-newer` than it, so the strip never touches a .so this install did not
# change the version of. See Dockerfile.v3197's own comment for the
# measured list of .so files a blanket strip corrupted before this fix.
RUN touch /tmp/.pre-pip-install && \
    /app/venv/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir \
        --constraint /tmp/v3197-constraints.txt \
        open-webui==0.11.4 && \
    find /app/venv -type f \( -name "*.so" -o -name "*.so.*" \) -newer /tmp/.pre-pip-install \
        -exec strip --strip-unneeded {} + 2>/dev/null || true && \
    find /app/venv -name "*.pyc" -delete && \
    find /app/venv -name "__pycache__" -type d -exec rm -rf {} + && \
    rm -rf /root/.cache /tmp/*.txt /tmp/v3197-constraints.txt /tmp/.pre-pip-install /var/tmp/*

# =============================================================================
# Stage: rc — v3.1.9.9's actual code, on top of the rollback stage above so
# every layer below this point is IDENTICAL to local/zla:v31910-rollback
# (and therefore shares layers with any pod that only ever ran the rollback
# stage — only what's added below is a new pull).
# =============================================================================
FROM rollback AS rc

# Memory-budget defaults. The full Dockerfile (lines ~436/486/495) sets these;
# prod's image predates them and bakes 0.6 / 6230 / unset. All .8 reviews ran with
# these values. At 6230 the reuse stand-in ceiling sits below her ~9k hierarchy, so
# the reuse path (and most of .8's speedup) never fires (final RC check).
ENV COMPACTOR_INJECTION_BUDGET_FRACTION="0.75"
ENV COMPACTOR_SUMMARY_BLOCK_MAX_TOKENS="15000"
ENV COMPACTOR_STANDIN_BUDGET_FRACTION="1.0"

# Scroll-jump CSS fix (Dockerfile.v3197's own step, copied verbatim: same
# idempotency guard, same "refuse if the target file is missing" checks,
# same append-not-replace behavior, same final grep assertions). Needed
# again here because this stage's OpenWebUI install is the SAME pip install
# as the rollback stage above — `pip install open-webui` always ships both
# custom.css files empty — so the fix does not carry over from anywhere
# else; it has to be (re-)applied on this exact venv, same as .7 applied it
# on its own.
COPY docker/v3197-custom.css /tmp/v3197-custom.css
RUN set -eu; \
    P=/app/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/open_webui; \
    F1="$P/frontend/static/custom.css"; \
    F2="$P/static/custom.css"; \
    for f in "$F1" "$F2"; do \
        if [ ! -f "$f" ]; then \
            echo "v31910-custom-css: expected target file missing: $f" >&2; \
            exit 1; \
        fi; \
    done; \
    for f in "$F1" "$F2"; do \
        if grep -q "overflow-anchor:none !important" "$f"; then \
            echo "v31910-custom-css: rules already present in $f, not re-appending"; \
        else \
            printf '\n' >> "$f"; \
            cat /tmp/v3197-custom.css >> "$f"; \
            echo "v31910-custom-css: appended rules to $f"; \
        fi; \
    done; \
    grep -q "overflow-anchor:none !important" "$F1"; \
    grep -q "overflow-anchor:none !important" "$F2"; \
    grep -q "content-visibility:visible !important" "$F1"; \
    grep -q "content-visibility:visible !important" "$F2"; \
    rm -f /tmp/v3197-custom.css

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compactor sources — EVERY non-test compactor/*.py module (29 files;
# `ls compactor/*.py | grep -v test_` confirmed to match this list
# 2026-09-27). Prod's own /opt/compactor tree (f3fafa3e, plain v3.1.9)
# predates request tracing and the word-ban file-deploy/warm-up runtime
# entirely, and has none of the .8-era fixes to the others either, so ALL
# 29 are new bytes on top of the rollback stage, not just the two new-in-.8
# modules (reqctx.py, wordban_runtime.py) called out below.
#
# compactor/requirements.txt pins opencv-python-headless; see the header comment.
RUN /opt/compactor-venv/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir --no-deps opencv-python-headless==5.0.0.93 \
 && /opt/compactor-venv/bin/pip check \
 && /opt/compactor-venv/bin/python -c "import cv2; print('cv2', cv2.__version__)"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
COPY compactor/main.py /opt/compactor/main.py
COPY compactor/envcfg.py /opt/compactor/envcfg.py
COPY compactor/memory.py /opt/compactor/memory.py
COPY compactor/facts.py /opt/compactor/facts.py
COPY compactor/allocator.py /opt/compactor/allocator.py
COPY compactor/continuity.py /opt/compactor/continuity.py
COPY compactor/backfill.py /opt/compactor/backfill.py
COPY compactor/retrieval.py /opt/compactor/retrieval.py
COPY compactor/summarizer.py /opt/compactor/summarizer.py
COPY compactor/health.py /opt/compactor/health.py
COPY compactor/selftest.py /opt/compactor/selftest.py
COPY compactor/portability.py /opt/compactor/portability.py
COPY compactor/dedup.py /opt/compactor/dedup.py
COPY compactor/commands.py /opt/compactor/commands.py
COPY compactor/persona.py /opt/compactor/persona.py
COPY compactor/backup.py /opt/compactor/backup.py
COPY compactor/degrade.py /opt/compactor/degrade.py
COPY compactor/bgwork.py /opt/compactor/bgwork.py
COPY compactor/textclean.py /opt/compactor/textclean.py
COPY compactor/tokens.py /opt/compactor/tokens.py
COPY compactor/tokenhealth.py /opt/compactor/tokenhealth.py
COPY compactor/tailhealth.py /opt/compactor/tailhealth.py
COPY compactor/webuidb.py /opt/compactor/webuidb.py
COPY compactor/logsetup.py /opt/compactor/logsetup.py
COPY compactor/alert.py /opt/compactor/alert.py
# New in .8 (request tracing, committed b9b6839):
COPY compactor/reqctx.py /opt/compactor/reqctx.py
# New in .8 (word ban from a file, injected by the compactor, committed
# 04c9f15 / 07d8987):
COPY compactor/wordban_runtime.py /opt/compactor/wordban_runtime.py
# New in .9 (uploads backup, merged from feature/v3.1.9.8-uploads d586fc7):
# the separate, incremental mirror of /data/openwebui/uploads (her
# photos) — see CHANGELOG.md [3.1.9.9]. scripts/uploads-backup.py (the
# operator CLI) is already baked by the `COPY scripts/` line below.
COPY compactor/uploads_backup.py /opt/compactor/uploads_backup.py
# New in .10 (per-message chat journal, STORAGE_ROOT/journal/<conv>.jsonl;
# see CHANGELOG.md [3.1.9.10]). scripts/chat-journal.py (the read-only
# inspector) is baked by the `COPY scripts/` line below.
COPY compactor/chatjournal.py /opt/compactor/chatjournal.py

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# stt/, tts/, clean-models.sh: NOT copied. `docker cp`'d out of a throwaway
# container of f3fafa3e1949 and `cmp`'d byte-identical against this tree
# (stt/server.py, stt/requirements.txt, tts/server.py, tts/requirements.txt,
# clean-models.sh — 2026-09-27); only the *_test.py files under stt/ and
# tts/ differ, and those never ship in the image (test files aren't COPYd
# by any Dockerfile in this repo). Prod's own copies are already correct.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# ops/ and scripts/ — bakes the operator tooling and every repair script
# onto the pod at /opt/zl-repo, so no `git clone` is needed for `zl`,
# `ops/bootstrap.sh --boot`, or any scripts/*.py runbook step (fixes N3
# from the word-ban-deploy review: word-ban-deploy.py was not in the image
# before). COPY preserves the source file's mode bit-for-bit (confirmed
# against `git ls-files -s`). .dockerignore excludes __pycache__/*.pyc at
# EVERY depth (fixed 2026-09-27 — the old bare `__pycache__/`/`*.pyc`
# patterns only matched at the build-context root, not recursively, unlike
# gitignore's implicit recursion), so these two directory COPYs cannot drag
# in stale bytecode from any nested package under ops/ or scripts/.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
COPY ops/ /opt/zl-repo/ops/
COPY scripts/ /opt/zl-repo/scripts/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# entrypoint.sh and supervisord.conf — CONFIRMED TO DIFFER from prod's own
# copies (docker cp + diff against a throwaway container of f3fafa3e1949,
# 2026-09-27, not assumed from the old v3197-vs-c1295894 diff): entrypoint.sh
# carries the D12/M-2 DATABASE_URL gate checks (absent from prod's plain
# v3.1.9 copy) plus everything else .7 changed; supervisord.conf carries
# the new [program:zl-ops] stanza (task 2) on top of every other .7/.8
# change. Both COPYd below. The base Dockerfile's own entrypoint.sh ships
# checked in at mode 644 (git does not track its execute bit), so COPY
# alone does not make this fresh copy executable — `chmod +x` is required
# again here, exactly as Dockerfile.v3197 documents.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
COPY entrypoint.sh /entrypoint.sh
RUN chmod +x /entrypoint.sh
COPY supervisord.conf /etc/supervisor/conf.d/supervisord.conf

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Import guard (mistakes log, 2026-09-24: ".8 was committed with two
# undefined names and no tests... the missing-symbol class recurred").
# Explicitly imports EVERY compactor module by the same bare name
# supervisord's `directory=/opt/compactor` + uvicorn give it at runtime —
# not just main's transitive closure — so a module that main.py never
# imports (a future orphaned file, or a typo'd COPY destination above)
# cannot hide behind "main imported fine". Fails the BUILD, not
# production, offline and network-free by construction so it cannot
# flake.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
RUN cd /opt/compactor && \
    MODEL_REPO=buildguard VLLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1 \
    HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 \
    COMPACTOR_STORAGE_ROOT=/tmp/buildguard LOG_DIR=/tmp/buildguard \
    /opt/compactor-venv/bin/python -c \
      "import main, envcfg, memory, facts, allocator, continuity, \
backfill, retrieval, summarizer, health, selftest, portability, dedup, \
commands, persona, backup, degrade, bgwork, textclean, tokens, \
tokenhealth, tailhealth, webuidb, logsetup, alert, reqctx, \
wordban_runtime, uploads_backup, chatjournal; \
       print('v31910 import guard: all 29 compactor modules import from the image')" \
    && rm -rf /tmp/buildguard /opt/compactor/__pycache__

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLOUDFLARED — v3.1.9.9: gives her OpenWebUI a stable
# https://ai.revelationsaints.com URL via a Cloudflare Tunnel, instead of
# the RunPod proxy URL (which keeps working alongside it during the
# transition — see RUNBOOK_CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL.md). Baked here, in the `rc`
# stage only — NOT in `rollback` (rolling a .9 deploy back also rolls back
# the tunnel; the rollback target is defined as "what a pod running today
# would fall back to", and today's pod has no tunnel).
#
# Pinned by version AND sha256, downloaded over HTTPS and verified with
# `sha256sum -c` before anything trusts the bytes — the same doctrine as
# every other pinned binary/wheel in this file. The digest is the exact
# value GitHub's release API reports for this asset
# (https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/cloudflared/releases/tags/2026.9.3
# -> assets[] where name == "cloudflared-linux-amd64" -> "digest"), verified
# independently on 2026-09-27 by downloading the asset and running
# `sha256sum` on it directly — two different retrieval paths agreeing, not
# just trusting the API's own digest field.
#   version:  2026.9.3
#   asset:    cloudflared-linux-amd64
#   sha256:   77e26d8d900e0b8469f416239d14b5f296525fdf79fee6f511ef55609e3fbac2
#
# `cloudflared --version` as a build check: proves the binary is not just
# present but actually executes (right architecture, not truncated by a
# failed download that curl still exited 0 for, etc.) — the same reasoning
# as the `python -c "import cv2..."` check on opencv-python-headless above.
RUN set -eu; \
    CLOUDFLARED_VERSION="2026.9.3"; \
    CLOUDFLARED_SHA256="77e26d8d900e0b8469f416239d14b5f296525fdf79fee6f511ef55609e3fbac2"; \
    curl -fsSL -o /tmp/cloudflared \
        "https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared/releases/download/${CLOUDFLARED_VERSION}/cloudflared-linux-amd64"; \
    echo "${CLOUDFLARED_SHA256}  /tmp/cloudflared" | sha256sum -c -; \
    install -m 755 /tmp/cloudflared /usr/local/bin/cloudflared; \
    rm -f /tmp/cloudflared; \
    cloudflared --version

# docker/cloudflared-run.sh — the [program:cloudflared] entrypoint
# (supervisord.conf). Reads CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN from the inherited
# environment (a RunPod secret; see the runbook) and either runs the
# tunnel or exits 0 with a one-line log when the token is absent — see
# that script's own header for the full reasoning. `chmod +x` for the same
# reason entrypoint.sh needs it above: this repo does not track execute
# bits, so a fresh COPY is not executable until told to be.
COPY docker/cloudflared-run.sh /opt/cloudflared-run.sh
RUN chmod +x /opt/cloudflared-run.sh
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# File-identity check: NOT done here at build time. Chose to do it in
# scripts/rc-boot-test-v3199.sh (task 4) instead, and explain why:
#
# A build-time RUN step can only compare bytes that came from THIS SAME
# build context against other bytes copied from THAT SAME build context —
# by construction, within one `docker build` invocation, a COPY'd file and
# the working-tree file it came from are the same read, so a manifest
# generated and checked inside this one build proves Docker's COPY did not
# corrupt bytes (already guaranteed) and nothing more. It cannot catch the
# failure mode that actually matters here: an image built from an OLDER
# tree being reused/retagged later while the working tree moved on (a
# stale local/zla:v31910-rc silently answering for a newer commit), or a
# COPY line whose destination path was hand-edited to something that
# LOOKS right but no longer matches what ships. Both of those are only
# detectable by comparing the file INSIDE A RUNNING CONTAINER against the
# CURRENT git tree, at TEST time, after the image already exists — which
# is exactly the sha256 check scripts/rc-boot-test-v3199.sh performs
# against /opt/compactor and the ops/scripts baked paths on the booted
# container. The import guard above already gives the build-time
# fast-fail this stage could add (a missing/renamed module breaks the
# build); the tree-identity property additionally needs is a test-time,
# not build-time, property.
